  abstract = {The proceedings contain 94 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Multimedia Modeling. The topics include: A Hierarchical Multi-scale Attention Enhancement Method forÂ Micro-expression Recognition: FromÂ Channel Modulation toÂ Spatial-Scale Fusion; food Recognition withÂ Visual Language Models: Search Re-ranking orÂ Retrieval-Augmented Generation?; preface; trackPhys: Learning Transferable Physiological Representations forÂ Motion-Robust Heart Rate andÂ 3D Mask Attack Detection; epistemic Uncertainty Guided Bayesian Neural Network forÂ Cardiac Image Registration; TF-AttNet:An Efficient Time-Frequency Structure Modeling For Low-Complexity Acoustic Scene Classification; SPDGS: Spatial Pruning and Depth Priors for Sparse-View 3D Gaussian Splatting; SMLA-YOLO: Efficient Multiscale Small Defect Detection in Wind Turbine Blades via Dynamic Feature Calibration; SFL-Net: Synergistic Spatial-Frequency Learning forÂ Medical Image Segmentation; multi-view Interaction Network withÂ Guided Contrastive Learning forÂ Multimodal Summarization; PGS-YOLO: A Lightweight and Accurate Framework for Aerial Small Object Detection in Urban Environments; DRA-YOLO: Dynamic Receptive-Field Attention andÂ Dual-Gated Upsampling Model forÂ Aerial Object Detection; dynamic Spectral Fusion andÂ Causal Graph Propagation forÂ Multimodal Recommendation; MAF3Net: Multiscale Attention andÂ Frequency Domain Feature Fusion forÂ Oracle Cross-Domain Recognition Networks; Can AI Capture Emotion? A Study onÂ Human Emotional Perception andÂ Response toÂ AI-Generated andÂ Human-Composed Pop Music; Dual-LoRA andÂ Quality-Enhanced Pseudo Replay forÂ Multimodal Continual Food Learning; benchmarking Gaslighting Negation Attacks Against Reasoning Models; multimodal Personality Trait Recognition viaÂ Spatiotemporal Modeling andÂ Dual-Stage Fusion; WES2P: Wavelet-Enhanced SAM2 forÂ Automatic Polyp Segmentation; FACER: Evaluating andÂ Enhancing Explainable Feature-Level Robustness viaÂ Causal